[2026-09-12T17:02:48.151] Cog0  BD-NOTE,the library isp_bldc_motor IS linked and is probed passively using testSetup() and getBoardType() -- no driver cog is started
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.152] Cog0  BD-NOTE,this binary contains no phase 2 motion code -- rebuild with -D DETECT_PHASE2 to add the cog-running sweeps
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.153] Cog0  BD-NOTE,the panic procedure at this bench is PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY -- emergencyCutoff() self-cancels in about 250 ms (finding S-4)
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.154] Cog0  BD-NOTE,the gate on phase 2 is compile-time only -- there is no keypress and no runtime branch anywhere in this binary
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.156] Cog0  BD-NOTE,BD-GATE answer and BD-BUILD phase2_compiled carry the same fact from two places and MUST agree; a disagreement voids the run
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.158] Cog0  BD-NOTE,sweeping a group briefly drives its base+4; with the boards at RIGHT P16_P31 and LEFT P32_P47 the gate-adjacent sense pins are P28 (right board base+12) and P44 (left board base+12)
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.159] Cog0  BD-NOTE,all six groups may be swept RAIL-OFF: P2 pins are inputs at reset so all six gate inputs already sit floating whenever no driver cog runs
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.161] Cog0  BD-NOTE,and rail-off means no bus voltage and therefore no shoot-through path whatever the gate driver does with a floating complementary input
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.162] Cog0  BD-NOTE,a RAIL-ON run should use -D DETECT_NO_TAIL which drops the two gate-adjacent tail groups
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.163] Cog0  BD-NOTE,P44 is PINS_P40_P55's sense pin and IS the LEFT board's W low-side gate input -- it is NOT unconnected; the calibration pin is P15, which is outside both board ranges
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.164] Cog0  BD-NOTE,VOID RULE: a log with no BD-BANNER or with cfg_id not equal to BENCH or with BD-CLK match 0 is VOID -- not suspect but void
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.166] Cog0  BD-NOTE,VOID RULE: any BD-ENUM match 0 voids the run -- the local pin-group table has drifted from the library's
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.167] Cog0  BD-NOTE,SUM RULE: sum 0 is real data on a Rev A board and is also what a loop that never executed produces
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.168] Cog0  BD-NOTE,SUM RULE: sum 0 is trustworthy ONLY when sumtix is at least 500 -- 500 Spin2 pinreads cannot complete in under 500 ticks
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.169] Cog0  BD-NOTE,CAL RULE: BD-CAL is emitted three times against a pin held driven high so the loop can never exit early
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.171] Cog0  BD-NOTE,CAL RULE: if the three tix_per_iter values differ by more than a few percent then every sumtix and every fltix in this log is void
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.172] Cog0  BD-NOTE,CROSS-CHECK: iter and (fltix / tix_per_iter) are two independent routes to the same number; if they disagree the instrumentation is lying
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.173] Cog0  BD-NOTE,R1 NOTE: pre and post are each assembled from TWO 8-pin pinread calls (low half in bits 0-7 high half in bits 8-15)
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.175] Cog0  BD-NOTE,R1 NOTE: that split is required because ADDPINS cannot cross a 32-pin port boundary; pre and post are therefore NOT atomic
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.176] Cog0  BD-NOTE,R1 NOTE: the lost atomicity is acceptable because pre and post are context snapshots and are not the measured interval
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.177] Cog0  BD-NOTE,HALL: bits 5 6 and 7 of a pre field are pin_hall_u/v/w so with a motor plugged in a valid 3-bit hall code is objective evidence the rail is powered
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.179] Cog0  BD-NOTE,DIFF: take the A/B diff over ^BD- lines only and exclude everything between a BD-LIB mark begin and its matching mark end
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.180] Cog0  BD-NOTE,DIFF: that exclusion is required because the library's own output line count varies with its own verdict
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.181] Cog0  BD-NOTE,DIFF: logs from different build variants are not comparable -- compare a default-build log only against another default-build log
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.183] Cog0  BD-NOTE,LIBVRD: a bare abort returns 0 and is indistinguishable from a completed call so ABORT appears only for a valued abort
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.184] Cog0  BD-NOTE,LIBVRD: ground truth for an abort is the library's own ! ERROR: line inside the BD-LIB bracket
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.185] Cog0  BD-NOTE,UNREACHABLE: cold-after-a-cog-has-run is impossible in one power cycle by definition -- that is why every cog NONE cell is phase 1
[2026-09-12T17:02:48.186] Cog0  BD-NOTE,UNREACHABLE: and it is why phase 2 can never be re-run without a reset
